1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,174
This is a boarding party.

2
00:00:03,074 --> 00:00:06,117
The ship is alongside a dead hulk,

3
00:00:06,567 --> 00:00:11,785
and the people on the bridge have just gone aboard as themselves.

4
00:00:13,585 --> 00:00:17,498
Last time you played a scene somebody else wrote.

5
00:00:18,398 --> 00:00:22,746
Today you write your own: who goes, where they go,

6
00:00:23,196 --> 00:00:26,239
and the few lines that start it.

7
00:00:27,439 --> 00:00:34,396
First, who goes. I go to the end of my fact sheet and add a section,

8
00:00:34,846 --> 00:00:40,063
and the first line inside its fence is one bare word, crew.

9
00:00:40,963 --> 00:00:43,572
Then the ship these people crew,

10
00:00:44,022 --> 00:00:47,935
and a line that says the names are locked.

11
00:00:49,735 --> 00:00:52,778
Under it, one record for each person.

12
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:57,157
Each one says which console they sit at,

13
00:00:57,607 --> 00:01:00,650
what they look like, and their job.

14
00:01:01,550 --> 00:01:05,463
So whoever sits at Engineering tonight is Chief Okoro,

15
00:01:05,913 --> 00:01:08,957
on the bridge and aboard the hulk.

16
00:01:09,857 --> 00:01:12,900
There's one cast, and it's the crew.

17
00:01:14,100 --> 00:01:15,839
Now, where they go.

18
00:01:16,739 --> 00:01:19,783
A place is a section of rooms,

19
00:01:20,233 --> 00:01:24,580
and a room is the simplest record you've written yet.

20
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:27,639
It has no fence at all.

21
00:01:29,439 --> 00:01:35,091
One line that starts with a percent sign is what the party finds.

22
00:01:35,991 --> 00:01:40,774
Each line that starts with a dash is a way out:

23
00:01:41,224 --> 00:01:45,137
the words in square brackets go on a button,

24
00:01:45,587 --> 00:01:50,804
and the key in round brackets names the room it leads to.

25
00:01:52,604 --> 00:01:57,822
And this one has nothing in its round brackets. It leads nowhere,

26
00:01:58,272 --> 00:02:00,880
and taking it ends the visit.

27
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:04,689
I save, and I run lint,

28
00:02:05,139 --> 00:02:07,748
and for once it isn't clean.

29
00:02:08,648 --> 00:02:13,865
It says nothing in this mission reads a section with this key,

30
00:02:14,315 --> 00:02:17,793
so my rooms are never loaded. That's true.

31
00:02:18,693 --> 00:02:20,867
Nothing does read them yet.

32
00:02:21,317 --> 00:02:25,230
So I leave the key exactly as it is,

33
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:30,028
and I go and add the thing that reads it.

34
00:02:31,228 --> 00:02:32,967
Before that, two rules.

35
00:02:33,867 --> 00:02:36,911
One: every room has a way back.

36
00:02:37,811 --> 00:02:42,593
A room with no way out holds the party for good,

37
00:02:43,043 --> 00:02:45,217
and lint won't tell you.

38
00:02:47,017 --> 00:02:51,365
Two: the way home goes where leaving is a decision.

39
00:02:52,265 --> 00:02:55,309
One press of that button, by anyone,

40
00:02:55,759 --> 00:03:00,541
ends the visit for everybody, and the place isn't offered again.

41
00:03:01,441 --> 00:03:04,920
So it's in the room they arrive in,

42
00:03:05,370 --> 00:03:07,543
and nowhere else for now.

43
00:03:08,743 --> 00:03:15,265
Now the start. I add a quest of the kind you wrote in Class 1:

44
00:03:15,715 --> 00:03:19,628
bring the ship within five hundred of the hulk.

45
00:03:20,528 --> 00:03:23,137
The new line is this one.

46
00:03:23,587 --> 00:03:27,065
When the quest completes, it sends a signal,

47
00:03:27,515 --> 00:03:30,124
and I've named it board hulk.

48
00:03:31,924 --> 00:03:36,707
Then I open the story file, go to the very end,

49
00:03:37,157 --> 00:03:39,330
and paste one recipe card.

50
00:03:40,230 --> 00:03:41,970
I don't read it.

51
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:48,507
I change three things on it, and they're on the page: the signal's name,

52
00:03:48,957 --> 00:03:52,870
the key of the room the party arrives in,

53
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,928
and the name the crew sees.

54
00:03:57,728 --> 00:04:01,207
I run lint again, and now it's clean.

55
00:04:02,407 --> 00:04:08,059
I start the game with a server, a Helm and an Engineering console.

56
00:04:08,959 --> 00:04:12,437
And there's my name, before I've flown anywhere.

57
00:04:14,237 --> 00:04:16,846
I bring the ship in close,

58
00:04:17,296 --> 00:04:19,035
and the quest completes.

59
00:04:19,935 --> 00:04:22,543
On Engineering I open the handheld,

60
00:04:22,993 --> 00:04:28,211
and there's a Boarding Party tile offering The Hulk. I beam down.

61
00:04:30,011 --> 00:04:33,054
Now this console is the party's handheld.

62
00:04:33,504 --> 00:04:38,722
It says who I am, my job, and the room I'm in,

63
00:04:39,172 --> 00:04:44,824
and under that is my line, with a button for each way out.

64
00:04:45,724 --> 00:04:50,072
I go aft, and the page keeps what I've read.

65
00:04:50,972 --> 00:04:52,711
Back, forward, back again.

66
00:04:54,511 --> 00:04:57,554
And from the airlock, I go home,

67
00:04:58,004 --> 00:05:01,048
and the console is back at Engineering.

68
00:05:02,248 --> 00:05:08,335
Your turn. Add a fourth room, with a way in and a way back,

69
00:05:08,785 --> 00:05:15,741
and add a third person to your roster, at Helm, with a job you make up.

70
00:05:17,541 --> 00:05:19,715
Then break it on purpose.

71
00:05:20,165 --> 00:05:23,643
Delete the way back from your new room,

72
00:05:24,093 --> 00:05:27,137
run lint, and read the word clean.

73
00:05:28,037 --> 00:05:33,254
Then walk into that room, and see what your crew would see.

74
00:05:35,054 --> 00:05:38,098
Next time, everyone gets a different menu.
